#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Phase for the Amplitude-Phase Form for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b5b735d-63dc-59e6-b41c-77003c0e40a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333398} {:answer/id #uuid "57318f06-cd50-578b-ae0b-794fe204ec64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333782} {:answer/id #uuid "575d47bf-3cbd-57ee-92d6-60684fb5f9d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333788} {:answer/id #uuid "688f9863-4f33-5417-9de0-c09ccf5fcb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333949} {:answer/id #uuid "a0da0bdd-42a6-5ec1-a897-867603b5eeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0da0bdd-42a6-5ec1-a897-867603b5eeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334401} :answer-field/id #uuid "44d64f22-bb75-503b-b5b4-1ad2bd5bcbcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0c19689-c107-5415-8074-e35dadeefb3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65582" :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
